omething important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Read the paragraph and select all the adverbs of manner."}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le13ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le13ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le13ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le13ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Are men and women raising their children equally? According to research, the answer is clearly no.\n<br><br>\nA study to find out how to help children become better students was repeated similarly in eleven countries around the world. The most interesting part of the study was about how much time fathers spend with their children."}, {"time": "17000", "image": "engenn6le13ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Surprisingly, fathers spend an average of less than one hour per day with their little ones. American fathers were the most generous with their time: they spent forty-two minutes on average. Fathers in Hong Kong spent less time: only six minutes."}, {"time": "32000", "image": "engenn6le13ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "Mothers, no matter which culture they come from, spend more time with their children, even when they work outside the home. American mothers spent the most time with their children, almost 11 hours. German and Nigerian women lovingly cared for their children an average of 10 hours per day. Belgian mothers spent the least amount of time (5.2 hours a day).\n<br><br>\nHave things dramatically changed since this study was conducted? Let me know what you think!"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Gender Issues"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Have Things Changed?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le13ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to raise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to care for children from babies until they become adults"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Are men and women raising their children equally?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about research on men and women."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "research"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the collection of academic studies on a topic"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: According to research, men do not spend as much time with their children."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "study"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an investigation on a topic; a piece of research"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The study was about how much time fathers spend with their children."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spend"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be with a person during a period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most interesting thing was about how much time fathers spend with their children."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "average"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the mathematical result of adding up the total amount divided by the number of items"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Fathers spend an average of less than one hour per day with their children."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "little ones"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "children"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Fathers spend an average of less than one hour per day with their little ones. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outside the home"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at a workplace (an office, clinic, school, etc.)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Mothers spend more time with their children, even when they work outside the home. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Adverbs of manner tell us how something happens. They are usually placed either after the main verb or after the object. Additionally, adverbs of manner can be found in past, present, and future tenses as well as in questions, and affirmative and negative sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\"><ul>  \t<li> Are men and women raising their children equally?</li> \t<li>According to research, the answer is clearly no.</li> \t<li>Surprisingly, fathers spend an average of less than one hour per day with their little ones.          Have things dramatically changed since this study was conducted?</li> \t</ul>   \t\t\t</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding -ly to an adjective:<br /><span class =\"strong\">Examples:  </span><br /><span class=\"italic\">Equal--->equally<br /> Surprising--->Surprisingly</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The words fast, hard, well and straight are exceptions. They are both, adjectives and adverbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"equal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"equally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"loving\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lovingly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dramatic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"dramatically\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"surprisingly\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"clear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"clearly\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Superlatives and Comparatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use comparatives and superlatives when we want to compare items based on a specific characteristic (adjective). <br /> We can also use these forms when we talk about comparison of quantity. Then the expressions are used with nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For the <span class =\"strong\">comparative</span>, we use the expression <span class =\"strong\">more</span>: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">Mothers spend more time with their children; Nigerian women lovingly cared for their children more hours per day.</span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we compare in terms of a lower degree, we use the expression <span class =\"strong\">less</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">Fathers spend less time with their children; there's less family time in the city.</span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " For the superlative, we use the expression <span class=\"strong\">the most</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">American mothers spent the most time with their children; American fathers were the most generous with their time.</span></li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When an item represents the lowest degree, we use the expression <span class =\"strong\">the least</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li><span class=\"italic\">Nigerian parents spend the least time with their children.</span></li>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I spend the most time with my family."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Families have less children these days."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Parents spend more time at work nowadays."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The study revealed the least expected results."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of 6 questions you want to find out about other people's families. For example, Who takes care of children? Who works outside the home?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask 10 people your questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down the results of your survey."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a graph, such as a bar graph, to display your results."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your graph to the class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a list of questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk to 10 people about their family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a graph."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the graph to the class."}]}]}